confirm.description:
Home Assistant will upload the packaged native agent through the currently configured maintenance API. SSH credentials are not needed. Active GUI and firewall patches are checked read-only first and refreshed only if they were already active and the packaged patch source changed. If you use in-house-only Ring Calls, also verify the Home Assistant user / in-house binary patch in the integration options after the update.

Installed: {installed_version} (API {installed_api_version}, bundle {installed_bundle_hash})
Packaged: {available_version} (API {available_api_version}, bundle {available_bundle_hash})
Update path: {update_path}
GUI patch status: {qml_patch_status}
Reason: {reason}

ssh_install.description:
This installed agent cannot update itself yet. Home Assistant will use these one-time SSH credentials to install the packaged agent, then refresh only active GUI and firewall patches when the packaged patch source changed. The SSH credentials are not stored. If you use in-house-only Ring Calls, also verify the Home Assistant user / in-house binary patch in the integration options after the update.

Installed: {installed_version} (API {installed_api_version}, bundle {installed_bundle_hash})
Packaged: {available_version} (API {available_api_version}, bundle {available_bundle_hash})
Update path: {update_path}
GUI patch status: {qml_patch_status}
Reason: {reason}
